Modifications
------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a fork of revfactory/harness (upstream v1.2.0). The following
changes were made by punkyade and are NOT part of the upstream project:

- Renamed the plugin to "myharness" and the marketplace to
  "myharness-marketplace"; repointed all ownership, repository, and
  support routing to punkyade/myharness.
- Removed upstream's project-specific claims and marketing material,
  including the A/B research results ("+60% average quality", n=15),
  the associated paper citation (Hwang, M. 2026), the harness-100
  catalog references, the ecosystem-positioning ("L3 Meta-Factory")
  and coexistence sections, the Star History chart, and the FAQ.
  These describe upstream's work and measurements, not this fork's.
- Removed the marketing landing page (index.html), its privacy policy
  (privacy.html), and unreferenced image assets.
- Removed _workspace/ (1,963 lines), upstream's internal launch and
  outreach working files — release audits, Show HN launch planning,
  awesome-list outreach targets, and marketing copy. This material
  documents upstream's own launch effort and has no bearing on this
  fork; it also restated the "+60%" claims removed above.
- Simplified README (EN/KO/JA) and CONTRIBUTING for single-maintainer
  use; removed response-time SLA commitments and the upstream
  maintainer roster, which this fork cannot honor.
- Fixed upstream documentation defects: inconsistent plugin install
  commands, a broken link to a non-existent document, placeholder
  links, SLA text citing a CI workflow that does not exist, and
  missing tables of contents in two reference files.

The core meta-skill content under skills/harness/ is substantially
upstream's work, carried over with the documentation fixes noted above.
